Let's start by merging the square roots:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{24b^3}\cdot\sqrt{40b^2}\cdot\sqrt{b^2}
&=\sqrt{24b^3\cdot 40b^2\cdot b^2}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{960b^7}
\end{align}$

Now we remove all perfect squares from inside the square root:

$\begin{align}
\sqrt{960b^7}
&=\sqrt{8^2\cdot 3\cdot 5\cdot \left(b^3\right)^2\cdot b}
\\\\
&=\sqrt{8^2}\cdot\sqrt{15}\cdot\sqrt{ \left(b^3\right)^2}\cdot \sqrt{b}
\\\\
&=8\cdot \sqrt{15}\cdot b^3\cdot \sqrt{b}
\\\\
&=8b^3\sqrt{15b}
\end{align}$
